# AUDIT LEDGER — one JSON object per line.
#
# A line records that a commit which touched a control was handed to an auditor
# that did not write it (CLAUDE.md rule 20). Fields:
#
#   commit   full or abbreviated sha (>= 7 chars)
#   auditor  what performed it — never the author of the commit
#   at       ISO timestamp
#   found    how many defects it returned, or 0
#   note     one line a later reader can act on
#
# WHAT A LINE DOES NOT MEAN. This file cannot tell a real audit from a line
# somebody typed, and it approves nothing. Exactly like `granted_by` in the
# override channel, its value is that an ABSENCE is visible — not that a
# presence is proof. Anybody reading it to decide whether the code is sound has
# misread it; read the audit.
#
# Report coverage with:  node scripts/check-audit-coverage.mjs
#
